{
  "$comment": [
    "Every icon Dray uses, mapped per platform. Generated by build/gen-icons.mjs into:",
    "  src/Dray.Core/Shell/Icons.g.cs        the IconRef enum + native resolution tables",
    "  src/Dray.Ui/wwwroot/icons/sprite.svg  the vendored sprite the WebView references",
    "",
    "MAUI.Sherpa put SF Symbol strings straight into the shared ToolbarAction contract, which",
    "forced GTK to keep a hand-written translation table plus pre-rendered PNGs plus Font Awesome",
    "aliases -- three naming schemes in one dictionary. Here the shared code names an IconRef and",
    "each platform resolves it, so a missing mapping fails the build.",
    "",
    "`sf` is an SF Symbol name (macOS chrome). `gtk` is an Adwaita icon name (GTK chrome).",
    "`svg` is the sprite geometry: a 24x24 viewBox, stroke-based, painted with currentColor.",
    "Windows chrome renders the sprite too -- inventing Segoe Fluent codepoints we cannot verify",
    "would be exactly the guesswork this file exists to remove."
  ],
  "geometry": {
    "viewBox": "0 0 24 24",
    "strokeWidth": 2,
    "linecap": "round",
    "linejoin": "round"
  },
